# Agreements

This directory holds executed agreements, MOUs, and subawards for
{{ org_name }}.

## What belongs here

- Fully executed agreements: MOUs, teaming agreements{% if federal_grants_focus %}, subaward and subrecipient agreements, CRADAs{% endif %}, vendor and consultant contracts above the routine-purchase threshold, and any other agreement your Delegation of Authority Policy requires the Board or Executive Director to track centrally.
- Executed documents only. Draft or unsigned agreements under negotiation do not belong here.

## How agreements get here

An agreement is added to this repository through the same governance
process as any other document (see `GOVERNANCE.md`): {{ "an" if vcs_platform == "gitlab" else "a" }}
{{ mr_term }} on the appropriate branch, reviewed and approved per the
Delegation of Authority Policy and, where the agreement itself requires
board approval, at the applicable quorum threshold.

## A note on privacy

This directory is a scaffold. It ships empty. Executed agreements
routinely contain counterparty PII, negotiated financial terms, and
confidentiality or non-disclosure obligations owed to a third party — not
just to your own organization.

**Your organization controls its own privacy posture for its rendered
repository, and its confidentiality obligations to counterparties are
independent of that choice.** If this repository is public, or a
counterparty's agreement contains terms you are not free to disclose, keep
the real, signed document in your organization's own **private**
repository and record only a pointer, summary, or redacted version here if
your governance process requires a public-facing trace of the agreement's
existence.

**Never contribute real agreements, or any other real adopted content,
back to the [Golden Records](https://github.com/USCouncil/golden-records)
commons.** That repository is a public, generic template — it must never
receive real organization data, and it certainly must never receive a
counterparty's confidential contract terms. This directory, in *your own*
rendered repository, is the right place for your real agreements; the
commons template is not.
